1
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:41,249
Promise, Chiara and I will really

2
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:44,335
work hard and practice
for our very special first dance.

3
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:45,628
- Let's see it!
- Yeah.

4
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:47,630
So cute!

5
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:55,513
I thought you were my friend.

6
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:58,683
I thought you always stood
for what was right.

7
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:00,143
I was wrong.

8
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:08,902
How can we be sure it's really Quintin?

9
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:11,154
There are other senators, right?

10
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:20,872
It's just strange, sweetheart.

11
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:23,208
I mean, I'm not exactly stiff
when I dance.

12
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:26,127
I can shake my hips and groove just fine.

13
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,128
But I don't know.

14
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,255
When it comes to couple dancing,

15
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:31,841
I just lose all my confidence.

16
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:33,051
I don't know why.

17
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,682
Come here, Mikoy.
I'll teach you how to dance.

18
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:45,188
No, your right!

19
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:50,235
Hand on her waist.

20
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:55,490
There you go! With feelings.

21
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:00,245
That's right. Right.

22
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:01,871
Come on, you two.

23
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:03,206
Stop butting in.

24
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:04,582
This is for couples only.

25
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:07,127
Oh, come on. Cut it out.

26
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:08,795
- Let's continue.
- Hey!

27
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:10,922
Sorry about them, Chiara.

28
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:12,882
They're just excited.

29
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:14,717
It's okay.

30
00:02:16,302 --> 00:02:18,179
You'd better get used to it.

31
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:22,517
It's not every day
a family member gets married.

32
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:25,019
How about you? Are you excited?

33
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:27,981
I am.

34
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:30,859
I'm just not used to this.

35
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:33,820
It's not like this back in Prague.

36
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:35,864
People are more formal,

37
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:38,199
more intimate,

38
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:40,368
and more reserved.

39
00:02:42,453 --> 00:02:43,872
Here, it feels like

40
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:47,292
the whole town is getting married.

41
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:54,632
You know, that's just how it is
here in the Philippines.

42
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:57,385
When one person is happy,
everyone celebrates,

43
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:00,388
and when one person has a problem,

44
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:02,473
everyone shares the burden.

45
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:04,767
You're still not used to it?

46
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:09,272
I'm just not used
to so many people preparing

47
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:11,149
and celebrating for us.

48
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:16,362
You know, you'd better get used to it

49
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:18,740
because you're family now.

50
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:23,453
And in this family, no one prepares alone.

51
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:28,917
Thank you, Mommy Tess.

52
00:03:29,834 --> 00:03:32,211
Thank you for welcoming me with open arms.

53
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:34,839
Tess!

54
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:38,509
That's Paula.
Looks like she's got some gossip.

55
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,220
- I'll go talk to her.
- Sure.

56
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:42,639
What is it?

57
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:47,310
- She always calls here.
- I wonder why.

58
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,236
Where am I?

59
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:58,279
Do you know him?

60
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,368
Yes.

61
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:04,786
What do you mean, yes?

62
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,330
Yes, he's my patient.

63
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:09,457
What's his illness?

64
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,044
I can't tell you.

65
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:14,837
And why not?

66
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:23,763
Don't you know who we are?

67
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,433
Don't you know
what we're capable of doing to you?

68
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,394
I won't break

69
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:32,230
my oath as a doctor.

70
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:35,692
Even if you tie me up, or even kill me.

71
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:43,032
Chiara.

72
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:45,368
I want to show you something.

73
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:55,712
Is this you?

74
00:04:58,131 --> 00:04:59,215
No.

75
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:01,175
Are you sure?

76
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:06,681
It really isn't me, Mario.
Please believe me.

77
00:05:09,892 --> 00:05:11,144
If it's not you,

78
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:13,896
then who is she?

79
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:34,542
The doctor is a man of principle.

80
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:36,210
All right, Doc.

81
00:05:36,836 --> 00:05:39,589
Let's put those principles to the test.

82
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,120
What's that?

83
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:15,666
It's my squishy toy. Keep it down.
I squeeze it when I'm anxious.

84
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,585
I'm not afraid of you.

85
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:21,255
It's like he knows we won't hurt him.

86
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:24,550
Like he knows we're good people now,
and we've turned over a new leaf.

87
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,969
He knows we're bluffing.
What do we do now?

88
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:29,931
If we can't torture him,

89
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:35,353
maybe you could rough him up,
just a little.

90
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:37,772
Easy there, partner.

91
00:06:37,855 --> 00:06:39,524
We might end up back in prison.

92
00:06:39,607 --> 00:06:43,319
That would ruin your blossoming romance
with Agent Sianong.

93
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:47,448
True.

94
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:50,868
Being a good person is hard.

95
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,041
What are you doing?

96
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,417
<i>Yo, yo, yo</i>

97
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,378
<i>Doc with the funky smell</i>

98
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:03,256
<i>Confidential or essential, spill it now!</i>

99
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:06,342
<i>Our patience is running out somehow!</i>

100
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:08,803
<i>Cool, calm, and collected? Not today</i>

101
00:07:08,886 --> 00:07:10,471
<i>Drop the bomb, drop the truth</i>

102
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:12,348
<i>While you're at it</i>
<i>Drop that wisdom tooth!</i>

103
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:15,685
That's enough!

104
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:17,478
This is worse than torture!

105
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,355
Do whatever you want. Just stop rapping!

106
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:23,109
That was just the intro, Doc.

107
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:27,822
Who’s that?

108
00:07:31,325 --> 00:07:32,201
Uncle Mario.

109
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:36,622
Can I post this?

110
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:40,001
It's great content.

111
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:43,254
I'm sure it'll go viral.
It'll be trending.

112
00:07:43,337 --> 00:07:44,505
Right?

113
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:45,882
Sure.

114
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:48,342
Who knows? Someone might recognize them.

115
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:51,762
Or if not, they'll recognize me.

116
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:53,931
- Yo!
- I'll go viral.

117
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:55,600
I'll gain more followers.

118
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:59,854
Oh, Rahmboy. Not everything
has to be posted.

119
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:01,105
This is an investigation.

120
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:02,273
If this gets out,

121
00:08:02,356 --> 00:08:06,527
it'll be much harder to find out
who this dangerous person really is.

122
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:08,112
The one with Manananggal blood.

123
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:09,989
Mikoy's right.

124
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:12,450
We can't let this slide.

125
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,206
Uh, Uncle Mario…

126
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:19,916
Mikoy. Chiara.

127
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:21,834
What?

128
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:22,793
I know now.

129
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:25,463
I have a suspect.

130
00:08:26,088 --> 00:08:27,131
Who?

131
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:28,925
- This is unbelievable.
- Who?

132
00:08:29,675 --> 00:08:30,676
There!

133
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,802
Who is it?

134
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:34,013
- Who?
- There! That's the one!

135
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,682
- Agent Alex?
- Agent Alex?

136
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:45,358
Agent Alex.

137
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:49,946
Is this you?

138
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:53,324
They're pointing at you.
They say you're the suspect.

139
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:58,412
You're the only "Agent Alex"
who's new around here.

140
00:08:58,496 --> 00:09:00,748
And the birds said…

141
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:02,792
- What birds?
- Us? Birds?

142
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:06,837
They said you're good at fighting.

143
00:09:07,463 --> 00:09:09,131
Of course! It's Alex!

144
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:10,925
She's really good!

145
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:13,803
Possible, possible.

146
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:16,889
It's also possible you're a Manananggal.

147
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:17,807
Manan…

148
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,809
Confess already. You're busted.

149
00:09:20,768 --> 00:09:23,646
Yes. Wait. What are you
even talking about?

150
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:25,815
Guys, leave Alex alone.

151
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:27,108
It's not her.

152
00:09:27,191 --> 00:09:28,859
Mikoy, how can you be so sure?

153
00:09:29,485 --> 00:09:32,113
First, they're different heights.

154
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:35,449
Second, Alex has way better posture.

155
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,497
You're sure that's not me, right?

156
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:43,833
Enough.

157
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:45,167
This isn't a guessing game.

158
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,586
It's an investigation.

159
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:49,755
Agent Alex.

160
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:52,258
What do you have to say

161
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:55,428
about the allegations
that you're the mysterious vigilante?

162
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:58,389
There!

163
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:05,146
Rahmboy.

164
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:09,150
Follow-up question. Do you have a twin?

165
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,901
Or maybe a split personality?

166
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:13,237
Or do you transform at midnight?

167
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:14,447
That's it!

168
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,450
Uncle Mario.

169
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:19,160
Can I arrest them now?

170
00:10:20,244 --> 00:10:21,078
- Mario.
- Uncle Mario.

171
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:22,121
- Go ahead!
- We were just kidding!

172
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:24,040
- Absolutely.
- You're in trouble!

173
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:25,374
Absolutely.

174
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:27,376
Mario, she can't possibly
be a Manananggal.

175
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,878
She's way too pretty!

176
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:30,588
- We've missed you.
- Oh, there.

177
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:34,258
The one beside you. That's her.

178
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:35,760
Alex!

179
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:36,844
Seriously!

180
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,645
<i>Promise you'll tell us</i>

181
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:47,188
<i>The truth and nothing but the truth?</i>

182
00:10:47,271 --> 00:10:49,440
- Okay.
- <i>No more, no less</i>

183
00:10:49,523 --> 00:10:51,776
<i>Or you'll lose your teeth!</i>

184
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:54,654
Fine!

185
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:55,905
Piece of cake!

186
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:58,407
You've got it all wrong.

187
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:03,329
The truth is, the senator isn't sick.

188
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:06,540
What he has…

189
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:09,377
is a dream.

190
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:18,886
<i>The truth is,</i>
<i>he's just trying to regrow his hair.</i>

191
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:33,025
There!

192
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:38,739
What happened?

193
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:41,992
I paid in full.
Why did only half of it grow back?

194
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:46,497
<i>Unfortunately, the medicine</i>
<i>isn't perfect yet.</i>

195
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:50,251
I've got bangs. On just one side.

196
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,129
But you're right.

197
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:56,799
Because I know his dream
of having a full head of hair,

198
00:11:57,466 --> 00:12:00,511
and he trusts me
with his other dreams as well.

199
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:03,639
And with his deepest secrets.

200
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:08,894
<i>What?</i>

201
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:11,730
Why did you make a move on Moraviano?

202
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:13,649
It's not time yet.

203
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:15,734
Enough. You've done enough.

204
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:19,655
If you can't clean this up,
you'd better pack your things too.

205
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:32,793
I'm sorry, Senator,
but it's still not working.

206
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:34,462
That's all right.

207
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:38,507
It doesn't have to be perfect.

208
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:44,138
You know, let them think

209
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:47,641
that we're shedding hair and going bald.

210
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:51,061
Meanwhile, we stay quiet

211
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:55,232
and rise when they're not looking.

212
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:56,942
Stronger,

213
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:59,278
more powerful,

214
00:12:59,904 --> 00:13:01,864
and more disciplined.

215
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:04,742
Until nothing can stop us.

216
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:11,790
I thought all he wanted back was his hair.

217
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:17,796
Turns out it's the Sinigang Cartel 2.0.

218
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:26,805
I'm sorry about what happened.

219
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,682
It shouldn't have come to that.

220
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:31,143
The guards who did that to you

221
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,229
have been taken off duty,

222
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:36,482
and I've returned
your entire Chilimansi stash.

223
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:37,650
Complete.

224
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:39,401
Thank you.

225
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:44,156
But that's not the only reason I'm here.

226
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:47,159
Someone wants to meet you.

227
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,161
Who?

228
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:54,208
Someone with many connections

229
00:13:55,584 --> 00:13:57,211
and great influence.

230
00:13:57,294 --> 00:14:02,550
Someone who can offer you more
than just Chilimansi.

231
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,301
Every flavor.

232
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:06,845
Every single flavor, Viktor.

233
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:08,639
He can give you all of them.

234
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:14,663
Are you here?

235
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,081
Are you following me?

236
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:39,897
This is too much, Sir Viktor.

237
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,024
We’re already trapped here,

238
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:44,360
and they still want
to make a deal with you.

239
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:47,988
Such long hair you have!

240
00:15:49,406 --> 00:15:51,158
What did they want?

241
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:55,788
But it seems like
we will find out very soon.

242
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:05,297
Mr. Valtrovi.

243
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:09,176
I’m just following orders.

244
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:13,430
What?

245
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:14,515
It’s okay.

246
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:37,079
What? Should we tell Agent Sianong?

247
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:39,248
Not yet.

248
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:43,085
- He just had crispy pork lunch.
- Huh?!

249
00:16:43,168 --> 00:16:44,503
He might get high blood.

250
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:47,965
He had crispy pork?

251
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:49,967
He didn’t even invite me.

252
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:54,221
Meanwhile, I was always cooking
for him at the safehouse.

253
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:57,599
Now that he has a girlfriend,
he's forgotten all about me.

254
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:07,443
Let’s say I’m not good with secrets.

255
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:10,487
What secret is that?

256
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:19,997
Well then, how much
crispy pork have you eaten?

257
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:27,588
Agent Alex!

258
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:30,257
Mikoy.

259
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:33,886
Are you sure

260
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,180
that’s not you?

261
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:41,101
Earlier, you were on my side,
and now you’re asking me.

262
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:48,400
That’s not really you.

263
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:52,529
I’m getting nervous.

264
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:55,032
Why?

265
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:59,745
I’m not the same waiter
you met in Prague, Alex.

266
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:01,705
I’ve learned so many things.

267
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:04,208
Why? What’s your theory?

268
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:09,880
La Morte Bianca is gone,
but not the Concordat.

269
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:14,760
Agent Alex, if someone followed us here,

270
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:18,597
I want to know as soon as possible,
before everything gets ruined.

271
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:26,313
Alex, I just want to get married.

272
00:18:27,481 --> 00:18:29,233
To start a new normal life.

273
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:32,986
Our life is okay here.

274
00:18:34,905 --> 00:18:35,906
Peaceful.

275
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,493
I don’t want anyone to ruin it.

276
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:50,420
You might not be admitting it,

277
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:53,132
but you are still able to retain
your insticts as an asset.

278
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:56,176
Sianong will be happy about it.

279
00:18:56,885 --> 00:18:59,596
I’ll see what I can do about this.

280
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,183
Thank you.

281
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:11,733
Thank you.

282
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:26,415
What did you do to him?

283
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:29,793
You kidnapped, tortured,
and abducted him. What is this?

284
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:32,045
Technically, nothing yet.

285
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:35,716
You’re right about the kidnapped,
but we just let him sit, that’s all.

286
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:38,343
We didn’t hurt him.

287
00:19:39,761 --> 00:19:41,513
That’s true.

288
00:19:42,014 --> 00:19:45,726
But please,
make him stop with his rapping.

289
00:19:45,809 --> 00:19:48,937
<i>Ouch, Doc!</i>

290
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:52,357
<i>Just tell us the truth or else…</i>

291
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:59,489
Fine. I’ll tell you the truth.

292
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:05,162
Okay, Doc, tell the whole truth
to Agent Sianong.

293
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:13,712
I will spill everything.

294
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,798
About senator Quintin.

295
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:35,442
This way.

296
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:48,330
Viktor Valtrovi!

297
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:21,196
All right, Sen.

298
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,114
‪CAFE ALLOR
‪RISTORANTE

299
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:34,376
<i>Suru.</i>

300
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:40,966
Agent Alex?

301
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:42,551
What did you need?

302
00:21:44,052 --> 00:21:45,971
I have someone
you have to background check.

303
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:48,849
Okay, who?

304
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:52,519
All the people here in Mikoy’s house.

305
00:21:52,602 --> 00:21:53,520
<i>All?</i>

306
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:55,605
Everyone.

307
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:57,816
From Captain Pepe to Rahmboy.

308
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:08,744
Thank you.

309
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:18,754
<i>Let’s see who amongst them</i>
<i>is the real vigilant.</i>

310
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:33,268
No one should find out about this.
Is that clear?

311
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:34,227
Understood, sir.

312
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:37,939
The person we are monitoring
is not just a simple Senator,

313
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:41,526
but a new syndicate
that is about to be born.

314
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:47,282
You are powerful enough
to take me outside,

315
00:22:47,365 --> 00:22:50,243
but you can’t make my case disappear?

316
00:22:50,327 --> 00:22:52,537
I can’t do that.

317
00:22:52,621 --> 00:22:56,333
But I can make something else disappear.

318
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:57,459
You.

319
00:23:04,007 --> 00:23:07,260
Since when are you taking
action without me knowing?

320
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:11,181
Since when have you and Cocoy

321
00:23:11,264 --> 00:23:14,684
been independently investigating
Senator Quintin?

322
00:23:19,981 --> 00:23:24,778
I can’t erase from my mind
that CCTV that Daddy Mario showed.

323
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:26,363
Forget about it.

324
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:29,783
Sweetheart, that person
is not just someone else.

325
00:23:29,866 --> 00:23:33,829
It seems like that person
has the same moves as me and Donatelo.

326
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:38,500
I'm starting to think we might have been
at the same training in Sicily.
